        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall the root श्रथ meaning \"weakness\" (दौर्बल्ये) in the curadi class of the Dhatupatha, cross-checking it against similar entries like ग्रन्थ (to tie/bind) in that same section.\n\nदौर्बल्ये\" belongs to the adanta (कथादि) group, so श्रथ + णिच् drops the final अ (अतो लोपः) without guṇa/vṛddhi since that lopa is sthānivat, giving श्रथयति — thus the conditional form अश्रथयिष्यावः. I'm confirming that even if this were the non-adanta root श्रथ meaning प्रयत्न (giving श्राथयति), the intended sense here is दौर्बल्ये, so the adanta form श्रथयति (ubhayapada, parasmaipada kartari) is correct, leading to अश्रथय...\n\n",
